  "manuscript_text": "Across the LLM judges, posterior means ranged from 3.863 to 4.514 for novelty and from 1.418 to 3.471 for significance, whereas testability estimates ranged from -0.906 to -0.571. For every LLM judge and dimension, the 95% HDI excluded zero, and the estimated posterior probability within the prespecified region of practical equivalence was 0.000. Direct posterior comparisons with the human estimates produced mean differences of 3.791-4.442 for novelty, 1.376-3.429 for significance, and -0.875 to -0.540 for testability. All nine 95% HDIs excluded zero. Model-implied tie probabilities at equal latent preference ranged from 1.0% to 3.3% for novelty, 0.4% to 0.9% for significance, and 0.4% to 3.7% for testability, compared with 16.5%, 20.2%, and 23.5% for human experts.",
